      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1915-10-23_WidnesExaminer_art0001" n="art0001">
        <p>The I(thgsvet•tis Patrick Craham, arson; %%Mita Edward Hargreaves, larceny of a postal iiuket; Joseph Nami Brown, manslaughter; Bridget Dryhurst, bigamy; Thomas Selwyn Johnson, perjury; Young Hill, murder; Cather- ine Alice Jones and another, bigamy and aiding and abetting; Patrick Donovan, Obigamy; Michael Smyth, criminal assault; Robert Henry Butler, bigamy; James Fleming, criminal assault; Ludwig Kahn and another, conspiracy, Lc.; Charles Arnold Tiller, larcenyi.Daniel Way and another,' coOr•ipacy, &amp;c.; David Lunn, per- jury; John Hollanet criminal assault; Alfred Roberts, housebreaking, Lc.; Arthur Edward false pretences; John Devonport, criminal assault; Robert George Leigh, larceny bf a postal packet; Cohn Archibald Mungo Park and another, false protences, &amp;c.; Elizabeth Mil- lington, wounding; Alice Emms, murder; John Grogan, bigamy; Alexander Schamsonoff and others, conspiracy, &amp;c.; Arthur Carson, larceny Of a postal packet; Elizabeth Blades, libel; Robert Winstanley Fielden, bigamy;</p>
        <p>And 'all other -Cases.</p>
        <p>All Indictments settled by Counsel forwarded to me Engrossed and Abstro,co.. The foregoing Regulations will be stritly en- forced, and persons making default in the observance of them will be liable tb have their costs disallowed. HERBERT Clerk of Assize. Office of Clerk of Assize, Preston, ___ 20th October, 1915. _ _</p>
        <p>All Depositions in cases for trial, together with Recognisances and Inquisitions, must be for- warded IMMEDIATELY" to me at Preston, otherwise the cost of tlieln may be disallowed.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1915-10-23_WidnesExaminer_art0002" n="art0002">
        <head>Wanted.—Public Officers.</head>
        <p>Wanted.—Public Officers.</p>
        <p>COUNTY BOROUGEt OF WARRINOVON. EDUCATION COMMITTEE.. The Committee invite applicatifts from. MARRIED WOMEN TEACHERS Vlio are pre- pared to act as SUPPLY TEAVHERS during the absence of assistant masters on military service. Salary according to the Obininittee's scale. Forms of application may be obtained from the undersigned. J. MOORE MURRAY. M.Sc., _ Secretary and Director.</p>
        <p>Education Office, Sankey-street, Warrington, 22nd October, 015.</p>
        <p>Mr Moeatta swot Robert Davies &amp; Co.. 14th con OlO 0 niployes Longford Gas Works, sth contribution ' 0 811</p>
        <p>Mrs. Harriet Fairclough .. F.W.G. Classes 6 &amp; 7, Beamont Girls' School, sth contribution H.F.03 0 _ _ _ .</p>
        <p>Bridge-street Collecting Box Market Gate Collecting Box</p>
        <p>62913 0</p>
        <p>Week's contributions: to October 22, £l4 Os. 7d. CONTRIBUTIONS to the various RELIEF FUNDS may be sent to the MAYOR, or to Mr. JOHN FAIRITURST, Bank House, Warrington.</p>
      </div>
