        <p>twill tell you of one of my traves up to tii:o trenches. -I was 'told off' to take rations up Ito Clarke's company, which on this particular zuning, I am sorry to soy, were very unfor- -1 tanate, for a shell 1)10* atnotuist thaw Ithit? they were having breakfast, aria killed tvillllfid. .nded about thirteen. I had just t'lirt!Yet.t [ Trie..6 fittioiz when a shell burst not fifteen yards ittWerj froth my Pker• ,</p>
        <p>NOVes Of Wan4nton Ws. "Nei 464 i you would like fo hear something about th irrington lads. 'Well, Buckley was not so well, Promoted him head cook, and he is mag 'Satisfactory progress at his new job. We are gt happy together, and have • all to be in readiness kr wnay be called upon any minute. Our time, ymay guess, drags rather heavy, and we are badly hi need of something to entertain us. We aYe not very good musicians, and I hope you *4l, ilpt think Us forward in asking if you cold&amp; Possibly send ns a second-hand gramophone. It would be very acceptable, as we are absolutely nt 'land's end.' No doubt you will have heard, of recent successes, in which our division has taliefi part. . big guns are firing away as I write, and doubt you will hear of somethini" else happening in a very short time."</p>
