        <p>E. If the War makes you feel de- pressed read "PUNCH",</p>
        <p>The second half opened very keenly, both teams attacking in turn, and after fifteen minutes' play the visitors' left-half secured the lead with a long shot. The Orford lads COD- tinned to have the best of the play, but G. Walters and his backs defended finely and pre- vented a score. Then the home team made a final rally to get on equal terms, but failed. Result: Orkrd Juniors, 2 goals; Mersey Juniors, 1 goal.</p>
        <p>HOWLEY JUNIORS V. BEWSEY.</p>
        <p>The above teams opposed each other for the first time on Saturday. The game opened very fast and even, Witton opening the score for the Juniors. After even play in midfield the same player scored again. By determined efforts tho Bewsey lads reduced the arrears. Half-time: Howley, 2 goals; Bewsey, 1 goal. The second portion was very similar in play as the first, Witton scoring the third goal and Challinor added the fourth. Result: Howley, 4 goals; Bewsey, 2 goals.</p>
        <p>MATCHES FOR TO-D.IY.</p>
        <p>FRIENDLY.</p>
        <p>EMMANUEL INSTITUTE V. WALTON A.F.C.</p>
        <p>_......_ _ At Victoria Park. Emmanuel Institute.—T. Knight; E. Crozier and S. Hughes (captain); F. Parr, E. Hardy and W. Ayres; A. Oakes, W. Booth, T. Hughes, A. N. Other and Wm. Eaton. Team meet at the Institute by 2.30;- kick-off 3 o'clock.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON AND DISTRICT JUNIOR LEAGUE. Bewsey V. Mersey Juniors. Bewsey Albion v. Latchford C.C. St. Blphin's v. Stockton Heath Scouts. Fairfield Juniors v. Howley. Orford v. Padgate C.L.B.</p>
        <p>TEAMS FOR TO-DAY.</p>
        <p>ELMWOOD CONGREGATIONALISTS v. PADDINGTON.</p>
        <p>On the King and Queen ground. Elmwood Congregationalists.—F. Roberts; Smith and Jos. Phenix; H. Oxley, H. Hazeldine (captain) and A. Holt; T. Wells, E. Kendrick, W. C. Ashton, J. Molyneux and H. L. Clayton. Reserves.—W. Littlewood, W. Gibson and H. Main. All players med at schoolroom at 2.30 prompt- Kick-off 3.15.</p>
        <p>ST. JOHN'S CHURCH v. PENKETH FRIENDS' SCHOOL.</p>
        <p>At Penketh. Kick-off 3 p.m. prompt. _ St. John's.—R. Shaw; R. Stark and C. Smith; .1 J. Bell, I'. Stringer (captain) and W. Car- ruthers; C. Lloyd, A. Nurse, R. Wright, E. Brown and A. Turner. The team to be at Penketh School not later than 2.45 p.m. Those walking must be at Rylands-street at 1.40 p.m. and take the car e. Sankey Bridges; then walk along the Liverpool- road to.Sankey Station (G.C. Railway). Cross the railway bridge, take the first turn to the left and so to the school and field.</p>
        <p>What! First Millionaire: Going to send your son to college? Second Millionaire: No. He is useless enough now.</p>
      </div>
