        <head>SALES BY AUCTION</head>
        <p>SALES BY AUCTION</p>
        <p>HENRY frAYWR, AUCTIONEER AND VALUER,</p>
        <p>ESTATE &amp; INSURANCE AGENT, 15, BOLD-STREET, WARRINGTON. Tel. 248.</p>
        <p>By Mr. HERBERT JOHNSON.</p>
        <p>LOCAL WAR FUNDS. SALE BY AUCTION. TO BE OPENED BY HIS WORSHIP THE MAYOR (ALDERMAN PETER PEACOCK), IN THE PARR HALL, at 2.30 p.m., on THURSDAY NEXT, the 28TH INST. lurß. HERBERT JOHNSON will SELL BY 1-7 - AUCTION a large and Valuable Col- lection of HOUSEHOLD APPOINTMENTS, Works of Art. Jewellery, Solid Silver, Sheffield Plate, Silver Plate, &amp;c., &amp;c., briefly comprising: Fine Mahogany Halls Stand, Semi-Billiard Table, Mahogany Overmantel, Large Framed Mirror, Brass Bedsteads, Gas Fires, new Rich- mond silent gas fire in Porcellanite enamel, with boiling burner, "The Louis"; Beautiful Water- colour Paintings, one by i Oswald Garside; En- gravings and Paintings n Oils, Buffalo Horns, large Rocking Horse, several Tons of Coal, Load of Wood Blocks, useful Luggage Cart, Waggon- ette, 2 Boilerettes, 2 Brass Mirrors and Sconces, Inlaid Letter Weight (from Christie's Sale), Gold Earrings, Gold Studs, Coral Necklace, Gold Buckle, Inlaid Jewel Casket, Gold Snake Brace- let with jewelled head, Gold Ring Topaz and Diamond, Gold Seal, Sheffield-plated Epergne, Silver Rose Bowl, Silver Tray, Finger Bowls, Copper Candle-holder, Embroidery, Indian Silver Filigree Card Case, magnificent solid Bronze Urn with fine decoration, Plated Toddy Kettle, Old Staffordshire Jug, thoroughbred New- • foundland bitch, half-a-dozen Garden Spades. I-cask Beer, quart Whisky, and useful and ornamental articles too numerous to mention. Mr. J. Canon Bardsley, of Padgate-lane, has offered an artificial denture to the value of .R 4 The Mayoress, Mrs. F. Lindley and Mrs. T. Locker will open Refreshment Stall on the premises during the Sale. Goods on view Wednesday, the 27th, from 10 till 5. Catalogues, 3d. each, may be had from Mem- bers of the Committee, the Hon. Secretary, Irvine Lister, Town Hall; or the Hon. Auctioneer. Terms: Cash. Auctioneer's Offices: Bewsey Chambers, Warrington. The Committee would like to call the atten- tion of the Public to the excellence of the above described, all of which, and a great number of other articles not mentioned, have been kindly given by local people, and the whole of the pro- ceeds will go to the benefit of the Funds.</p>
