        <p>OTICE OF AUDIT. .111 TO THE RATEPAYERS AND OWNERS OF PROPERTY IN THE URBAN DISTRICT OF LYMM, IN THE COUNTY OF CHESTER. WHEREAS, C. F. JORDISON, Esquire, the Dis- trict Auditor authorised by law to Audit the Accounts of the Receipts and Expenditure under the Public Health Act, 1875 of us, the URBAN DISTRICT COUNCIL for the above-named Dis- trict, has appointed 10 o'clock in the forenoon of FRIDAY, the 12th day of November, 1915, as the Time, and the COUNCIL OFFICES, LYMM, as the Place, at which the Audit of the said Accounts for the year ended at 31st March, 1915, will be made: WE, the said District Council, HEREBY GIVE NOTICE, in pursuance of the said Act, that the Audit of the said Accounts will be made at the Time and Place so appointed as aforesaid; that any Ratepayer or OwneD of Property in the said Dis- trict may be present at the Audit, and may make any objection to the said Accounts before the Auditor; and that a Copy of the said Accounts, duly made up and balanced, together with all the Rate Books, Account Books, Deeds, Contracts, Accounts, Vouchers, and Receipts mentioned or referred to in such Accounts, will be deposited in our Office at Whitbarrow, Lymm, on Wednesday, the 3rd day. of November, 1915, and will be open thereat, during office hours, until the said day of Audit, to the inspection of all persons interested, who will be at liberty to take copies "of or extracts from the same without fee or reward. Dated this 21st day of October. 1915. W. MULLARD. Clerk to the District Council. -.; 4 k. • LANCASHIRE VOLUNTEER REGIMENT. A PUBLIC MEETING will be held in the TOWN HALL, WARRINGTON, at 8 o'clock, on WEDNESDAY EVENING, the 27th instant, to FORM A COMMITTEE in connection with. the Warrington Area of the Lancashire Volun- teer Regiment. It is earnestly hoped that all interested will attend in order that the scheme should be a success. PETER PEACOCK, Mayor.</p>
