        <p>JUMPY NERVES. Jumpy nerves ! Quite right to blame the hurry-scurry of modern conditions for them. Not for a moment would one dispute that the principal cause of the run-down "jumpy" state which magnifies trifles into terrors is the stress and strain of present day living. But it is not so always. More often than is supposed wrecked nerves are due simply to Indigestion. You cannot expect to be free from nerve troubles if your nerves are not nourished ; and they can't be nourished if the blood is not enriched by thoroughly digested food. If you find you are not deriving the benefit from your food you should; if from this cause bodily vigour declines and you are in danger of becoming a nervous wreck—take Mother Seigel's Syrup.* No remedy before the public possesses its splendid powers of toning, strengthening, and stimulating the stomach, liver and bowels, on the healthy activity of which your vitality and nerve power so largely depends.</p>
